<title>UK: Royal &amp; Sun up on talk of cost savings.</title>
<headline>Royal &amp; Sun up on talk of cost savings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Royal &amp; Sun Alliance Insurance Group Plc Crept to a fresh record peak as the broad market tumbled amid optimism that the company's push to reduce costs had begun to pay off, dealers said.</p>
<p>That, against the background of ongoing bid talk in the industry, helped push the shares up 1p to 483-1/2p.</p>
<p>They have added about 10 percent since the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, Salomon Brothers named Sun &amp; Alliance stock as one of its preferred stocks for 1997.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
